Title: Verify agents must not use the main repo as their workspace
Created: 2026-05-13
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-05-13T00:10Z claude created — celebrate sweep after raid 122/114/125/130/138
2026-05-13T00:00Z claude note PR #176 opened — docs(verify): isolate verify/verify-gate agents in temp worktree

--- body ---
## Context

During raids, verify agents (`/verify`, `/verify-gate`) run `gh pr checkout <N>`
which switches **the main repo's** working directory to the PR branch. They make
fixes, push, then the main repo is left on the PR branch with staged/unstaged
noise. The orchestrator must then manually discard rogue changes and restore
`main` before proceeding.

Observed in this raid: beat.py MODEL_SONNET change, settings.json, healthcheck
SKILL.md, nightbeat-report SKILL.md, verify SKILL.md — all left as unstaged
changes in the main repo by verify agents that ran there.

The existing prompt mitigation ("task is complete after emitting the verdict")
does not prevent the checkout side-effect.

## Actions

1. In `/tmp` (or `.claude/worktrees/`), verify agents should always work in an
   isolated worktree or tmpdir — not the main repo checkout.

2. Option A — shallow clone: `gh pr checkout <N> --force` inside a temp directory
   created with `mktemp -d`. Tear down on exit. No impact on main repo.

3. Option B — worktree: Create `git worktree add /tmp/review-<N> <PR-branch>`,
   run verify there, `git worktree remove /tmp/review-<N>` on exit. Already done
   by the verify skill for review sub-agents (see `/tmp/review-158` pattern in
   `git worktree list`). Extend to the top-level skill invocation.

4. Update `skills/verify/SKILL.md` and `skills/verify-gate/SKILL.md` to document
   the isolation requirement and include the worktree setup/teardown step.

5. Add a pre-flight check: if `git branch --show-current` in the invocation
   directory is not `main`, warn and abort rather than switching branches.

## Relevant files

- `skills/verify/SKILL.md`
- `skills/verify-gate/SKILL.md`

## Test

After a `/verify` run on any PR, `git status` in the main repo returns clean
and `git branch --show-current` returns `main`.

## Exit criteria

- Running `/verify <N>` does not switch or dirty the main repo working directory.
- All fix commits land on the PR branch, not on main.
- Existing verify behaviour (adherence check, simplify, gate verdict) unchanged.
